MID_EV11_047_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_047_m01_001: Mom...did you know about Pop's illness?
MID_EV11_047_m01_002: Yes. The day you first came to visit, he told me\nhimself while we were alone.
MID_EV11_047_m01_003: He'd been suffering for a while, but he'd accepted\nthat death by execution was imminent.
MID_EV11_047_m01_004: And within his reprieve, he was able to raise you up\ninto a fine young man and return you to me.
MID_EV11_047_m01_005: He was proud that he lasted long enough to see\nthat through.
MID_EV11_047_m01_006: He asked me to keep his illness secret from you and\nyour friends.
MID_EV11_047_m01_007: Your father can be so stubborn... He didn't want to\nburden you with any extra worries.
MID_EV11_047_m01_035: <NCA>Get angry.
MID_EV11_047_m01_036: <NCB>Ask how she felt.
MID_EV11_047_m01_037: <ACA>I don't even know what to say to that. I'm so mad\nat him.
MID_EV11_047_m01_038: <ACA>As for me...I wasn't angry. I know that I'll outlive all\nmy loved ones.
MID_EV11_047_m01_008: <ACB>Were you OK with that? Weren't you sad?
MID_EV11_047_m01_009: <ACB>I was...prepared for it, right from the start.
MID_EV11_047_m01_010: We children of the progenitor god must live for\nthousands of years.
MID_EV11_047_m01_012: At times, I've thought that such longevity is like\nbeing locked in a cage.
MID_EV11_047_m01_011: And you, Cai, since you're half my blood, will live\nfor five hundred years, at least.
MID_EV11_047_m01_013: But when you've lived out your time, I'll continue on.
MID_EV11_047_m01_014: Castor is an ordinary mortal, so we don't get as much\ntime with him.
MID_EV11_047_m01_015: But this is something we can't avoid. However sad it\nis, we must accept the inevitability of it.
MID_EV11_047_m01_016: When I chose to become Castor's wife, and when I\nbore you, I knew this reality.
MID_EV11_047_m01_017: In this case, that hard truth plays out a little sooner\nthan expected.
MID_EV11_047_m01_018: That's not—how can you accept it?! That's just an\nexcuse for giving up!
MID_EV11_047_m01_019: Mom...it isn't right. This...isn't what I wanted to hear\nfrom you.
MID_EV11_047_m01_020: Wh—
MID_EV11_047_m01_021: Don't you want to be happy?! If not, why am I—
MID_EV11_047_m01_022: Sorry. I'm letting my emotions get the better of me.\nI know you're sad about all this, but...
MID_EV11_047_m01_023: Aurora, please forgive my intrusion. We have\nan emergency.
MID_EV11_047_m01_024: Centurio, what's all the fuss about?
MID_EV11_047_m01_025: There has been another disappearance within\nthe temple.
MID_EV11_047_m01_039: <NCA>Ask about the disappearance.
MID_EV11_047_m01_040: <NCB>Assume someone got lost.
MID_EV11_047_m01_026: <ACA>Disappearance? Someone vanished?
MID_EV11_047_m01_027: <ACA>Indeed. On several occasions, people have\nmysteriously vanished without a trace.
MID_EV11_047_m01_041: <ACB>You mean someone got lost? Well, it is a big\ntemple, right?
MID_EV11_047_m01_042: <ACB>That's not it, Cai. People have been mysteriously\ndisappearing without a trace.
MID_EV11_047_m01_028: It's gone on for nearly a century now, but we don't\nknow the cause.
MID_EV11_047_m01_029: Some miserable miscreants even spread rumors that\nit was the work of Aurora herself.
MID_EV11_047_m01_030: For Aurora's honor and for those who are missing,\nwe're doing everything we can to investigate.
MID_EV11_047_m01_031: But so far, we haven't found a single clue or\nrecovered any of the disappeared subjects.
MID_EV11_047_m01_032: Hmm... Cai, perhaps you could help Centurio search\nthe temple.
MID_EV11_047_m01_033: Simply take a look around yourself. Perhaps you\nwill see what others have overlooked.
MID_EV11_047_m01_034: Alright. I'll give it a try.
MID_EV11_048_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_048_m01_001: Hmm. There's something strange about this painting.
MID_EV11_048_m01_002: Strange how?
MID_EV11_048_m01_003: There are more figures in it than there were before.
MID_EV11_048_m01_004: Look here. There are more women in bridal gowns\nthan I remember.
MID_EV11_048_m01_005: Now that you mention it, this one looks kind of\nlike Ultand...
MID_EV11_048_m01_006: We must be imagining it. That figure's been part\nof the painting this whole time, right?
MID_EV11_048_m01_007: No, I'm sure of it. You know how good my\nmemory is.
MID_EV11_048_m01_008: Are you saying that Ultand is trapped inside\nthis painting?
MID_EV11_048_m01_009: Let me take a peek with my weird eye.
MID_EV11_048_m01_010: Hmm...
MID_EV11_048_m01_011: Huh? Aaaah!
MID_EV11_048_m01_012: Are you alright? Did you sense anything?
MID_EV11_048_m01_013: It feels like there are...people...inside the painting.\nIt's...buzzing.
MID_EV11_048_m01_014: Something is off. I'd better ask Mom about this.
MID_EV11_048_m01_015: People snatched away and trapped inside a painting?\nHow are we to believe that?
MID_EV11_048_m01_016: Don't be deceived, Aurora. Not by the falsehoods of\na man like Morrow!
MID_EV11_048_m01_017: I think it is as Cai says. Indeed, there's something\nvery strange about this painting.
MID_EV11_048_m01_018: Standing here, it gives me the same feeling as Cai's\neye. It's as if Balor's power is seeping out of it.
MID_EV11_048_m01_019: Are you saying Drake's treasures are involved?
MID_EV11_048_m01_020: Even so, it's difficult to fathom that Ultand was\nabducted within the walls of the temple.
MID_EV11_048_m01_021: A famous artist by the name of Zenzele painted this.\nHe was known as the Miracle Painter, I believe.
MID_EV11_048_m01_022: He took full advantage of his renown. The temples\ncommissioned many works from him.
MID_EV11_048_m01_023: It wouldn't surprise me to find his murals in\nevery temple.
MID_EV11_048_m01_024: But he vanished too, not long after he completed\nthis painting.
MID_EV11_048_m01_025: According to the temple records, that's when the\nother disappearances began as well.
MID_EV11_048_m01_026: Is the painting truly abducting people? If so, could\nthe painter Zenzele be one of its victims?
MID_EV11_048_m01_027: I'd like to do some further research on Zenzele and his\npainting here.
MID_EV11_048_m01_028: Cai, can you please bear with me awhile?
MID_EV11_048_m01_029: Ultand is a very dear friend to me too. We won't just\nabandon her.
MID_EV11_049_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_049_m01_001: Cai, everyone, thank you for coming today.
MID_EV11_049_m01_002: I've written to Father, to get more information about\nthe painting.
MID_EV11_049_m01_003: And Father was kind enough to quickly reply with a\nletter of his own.
MID_EV11_049_m01_004: Really? That's great!
MID_EV11_049_m01_005: It's just a few hand-written sentences, but it's been\ncenturies since we exchanged any words at all.
MID_EV11_049_m01_006: Did Lord Solel give you any clues?
MID_EV11_049_m01_007: Yes, I learned some things that you all need to know.
MID_EV11_049_m01_010: Zenzele was so skilled that he was said to capture\nthe very souls of his subjects.
MID_EV11_049_m01_011: He lived here in Dagsion with his wife and\nmany children.
MID_EV11_049_m01_012: But it appears that while he was working on a series\nof murals, his wife left him—as did his sanity.
MID_EV11_049_m01_013: What I'm most curious about is the mysterious\npaintbrush Zenzele was rumored to have. 
MID_EV11_049_m01_014: He'd been a rather unremarkable painter until one\nday something changed and he rapidly rose to fame.
MID_EV11_049_m01_015: All the stories point to the start of his success\ncoinciding with his acquisition of the brush.
MID_EV11_049_m01_016: Are you thinking his brush might be one of \nDrake's treasures?
MID_EV11_049_m01_017: I am. But it seems Zenzele never revealed how he\ngot it.
MID_EV11_049_m01_018: So what can I do to help? I want to rescue Ultand,\nthe sooner the better.
MID_EV11_049_m01_019: Thank you, Cai. But first let me entrust you\nwith this.
MID_EV11_049_m01_020: Hmm... This spear... It feels like it has an\nawesome power.
MID_EV11_049_m01_021: The Star Spear of Aurora is among the greatest\ntemple treasures known as Supreme Arcs.
MID_EV11_049_m01_022: I really ought to have given this to you when you\nwent to investigate Balor's temple.
MID_EV11_049_m01_023: Aurora! Are you sure about this? The handling of\nSupreme Arcs is governed by strict protocols.
MID_EV11_049_m01_024: If we're going to resolve this situation, the power\nof the spear is absolutely vital.
MID_EV11_049_m01_025: I've already obtained permission from Father.\nHe wrote that he'd leave it to my judgment.
MID_EV11_049_m01_026: Cai will be fine with it. After all, he's my son.
MID_EV11_049_m01_027: He's already learned the vulkan spear technique\nfrom Castor.
MID_EV11_049_m01_028: And I'm going to accompany him. I can't just send\nyou all into dangerous situations alone, you know.
MID_EV11_049_m01_029: As long as I remain in the temple, you'll have no\nobjections, will you, Centurio?
MID_EV11_080_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_080_m01_001: Cai, use the power of your eye to find the seal on\nthis painting.
MID_EV11_080_m01_002: If you can destroy the seal, we should be able to\nenter it.
MID_EV11_080_m01_003: Enter the painting... Is that even possible?
MID_EV11_080_m01_004: It must be. People have already been snatched away\nand imprisoned in it.
MID_EV11_080_m01_005: We must discover and remove the source of the\nproblem within the artwork itself.
MID_EV11_080_m01_006: If it is imbued with the power of Balor, the rules of\nthe underworld might be in effect.
MID_EV11_080_m01_007: But listen to me. Not one person has ever come back\nout of this painting.
MID_EV11_080_m01_008: We'll no doubt face many dangers. Cai, are you\ncertain you're comfortable with this?
MID_EV11_080_m01_022: <NCA>Say you're comfortable.
MID_EV11_080_m01_023: <NCB>Admit you're a little scared.
MID_EV11_080_m01_009: <ACA>Of course I am. We have to save Ultand, no matter\nwhat we're facing.
MID_EV11_080_m01_024: <ACB>To be honest, I'm a little scared. But I want to bring\nUltand back.
MID_EV11_080_m01_025: <ACB>I'm sorry to ask, but I'll need everyone's help if I'm\ngoing to make this work.
MID_EV11_080_m01_010: So here we go...
MID_EV11_080_m01_011: What is it, Cai? Can you see something?
MID_EV11_080_m01_012: Yes. I see... It looks like a big door. But it's shut.
MID_EV11_080_m01_013: The spear ought to open it. Try it, Cai.
MID_EV11_080_m01_014: {SetColor=Gray}Hmm? I've seen this somewhere before, haven't I?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_080_m01_015: {SetColor=Gray}That's it. It was the Herald of the Pale Raven's\nspear. At least, it looks like that one.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_080_m01_016: Look! The spear is glowing! The light is...beautiful.
MID_EV11_080_m01_017: Could it be that the Supreme Arc approves of Cai?
MID_EV11_080_m01_018: Spear. Please, open this door. I want to save Ultand.
MID_EV11_080_m01_019: Hyaaagh!
MID_EV11_080_m01_020: Look! The door opened! It's really there!
MID_EV11_080_m01_021: Hurry through! Centurio, please stay behind in case\nanything happens!
MID_EV11_050_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_050_m01_001: Cai! Aurora! I'm so happy you've returned, safe\nand sound.
MID_EV11_050_m01_002: Look! The paradise mural—it's broken up!
MID_EV11_050_m01_003: We won't have to worry about something like this\never happening again.
MID_EV11_050_m01_004: Who... Who are all these people?
MID_EV11_050_m01_005: Zenzele's family. And everyone else he trapped.\nThey all made it out!
MID_EV11_050_m01_006: Father! You escaped the painting! Thank goodness!\nIt's been so long...
MID_EV11_050_m01_007: You're... It can't be... Morrow? What's going on here?
MID_EV11_050_m01_008: Thank you so very much for helping me. I'm...\nI'm going home with my family.
MID_EV11_050_m01_009: What a story... I didn't expect to hear that Morrow\nwas actually Zenzele's descendant too.
MID_EV11_050_m01_010: Eighty years ago, his father brought the whole family\nhere. They were taken, all except for him.
MID_EV11_050_m01_011: He tried desperately to explain what happened, but\nno one believed him. They thought he was insane.
MID_EV11_050_m01_012: But he couldn't just leave things as they were. He\nkept coming back to the temple, alone, for decades.
MID_EV11_050_m01_013: His family members... His father... They're younger\nthan he is. But at least they're together again.
MID_EV11_050_m01_014: It must've been terrible for him, but he looks so\nhappy now.
MID_EV11_050_m01_015: He said, if he's got time to complain about the 80\nyears he lost, he's got time to enjoy this reunion.
MID_EV11_050_m01_016: It's incredible that Morrow can see things that way.
MID_EV11_050_m01_017: Thank you so much, Cai. Because of you, I made it\nback in one piece.
MID_EV11_050_m01_018: In that so-called "paradise," I was told I'd be part of\nthat creepy new family forever.
MID_EV11_050_m01_019: When I heard that, I thought I'd never see my loved\nones again. I was so scared and sad.
MID_EV11_050_m01_033: <NCA>Cheer her up.
MID_EV11_050_m01_020: Everything's alright now, Ultand. You'll see\nthem again.
MID_EV11_050_m01_021: I love hearing you talk about them. Your eyes light\nup, and you seem so happy.
MID_EV11_050_m01_022: You make me wanna put my family together too.
MID_EV11_050_m01_023: You're important to me, Ultand. I want you to\nbe happy.
MID_EV11_050_m01_024: I'm so glad we saved you.
MID_EV11_050_m01_025: Oh... Thank you so much, Cai!
MID_EV11_050_m01_026: Inside the painting, I kept hearing a strange voice.\nIt was as if it hated our world.
MID_EV11_050_m01_027: What's this? Zenzele's brush? It has the same energy\nas Cai's jewel.
MID_EV11_050_m01_028: Zenzele made himself famous with this brush, but it\ndidn't bring him happiness.
MID_EV11_050_m01_029: He lost his mind because he was obsessed with\nthoughts of his wife's betrayal.
MID_EV11_050_m01_030: He wanted a perfect paradise where no family\nmember could turn on him. So he painted one.
MID_EV11_050_m01_031: The brush's magic and its voice directed him to do\nevil things.
MID_EV11_050_m01_032: A paintbrush that ruins minds... I'd better keep this\nin the temple, since it's so dangerous.
MID_EV11_051_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_051_m01_001: You've been running your eyes over that with great\ninterest for a while. May I ask what it is?
MID_EV11_051_m01_002: It's happy news about the resolution of a problem\nthat has plagued me for a very long time.
MID_EV11_051_m01_003: It seems my daughter has brought an admirable\nconclusion to the disappearances in her temple.
MID_EV11_051_m01_004: This turn of events completely clears her of the\nsuspicions that have hung over her for 80 years.
MID_EV11_051_m01_005: The disappearances in Aurora's temple are\nresolved? So suddenly? How can that be?
MID_EV11_051_m01_006: They were perpetrated by the artist behind Eternal\nParadise, who used to be called the Miracle Painter.
MID_EV11_051_m01_007: It makes sense. He garnered much admiration. The\ntemples commissioned many paintings from him.
MID_EV11_051_m01_008: It may also be prudent to conduct a careful\ninvestigation of his other paintings.
MID_EV11_051_m01_009: Indeed. Please see to that. Hmm...
MID_EV11_051_m01_010: I never imagined that Aurora could tackle such a\nthorny issue. I suppose children do grow up.
MID_EV11_051_m01_011: You love that girl an awful lot, don't you?
MID_EV11_051_m01_012: I do. It's just...
MID_EV11_051_m01_013: Regarding the ugly rumor... I'm still uncertain how I\nought to proceed.
MID_EV11_051_m01_014: What do you think? Is it about time that we meet\nwith Aurora?
MID_EV11_051_m01_015: I'm certain she would be overjoyed to see you.
MID_EV11_051_m01_016: I...don't think it's possible just yet.
MID_EV11_051_m01_017: No? Is she not the child you carried in your belly\nand bore?
MID_EV11_051_m01_018: Perhaps if you speak with her, it will trigger the\nawakening of your sealed memories.
MID_EV11_051_m01_019: I'm frightened...of meeting her, that is. It seems as\nthough it would stir up something truly terrible.
MID_EV11_051_m01_020: Please, grant me a little more time. Let's keep things\nthe way they are for just one more year.
MID_EV11_051_m01_021: I understand. I won't move to change things with\nAurora, then, for a little while longer.
MID_EV11_051_m01_022: Still, resolved though it is, this was a bizarre incident.\nHow did such a thing happen?
MID_EV11_051_m01_023: Perhaps it would be good to stir things up and\nsee what comes of it.
MID_EV11_051_m01_024: It is I, Raksha. You summoned me, Lord Solel.
MID_EV11_051_m01_025: The mural of paradise at Aurora's temple... It was\nyou who introduced me to the artist, I recall.
MID_EV11_051_m01_026: I have been nothing but a disgrace to you, my lord.\nI could never have known he was so wicked.
MID_EV11_051_m01_027: Hmm? Well, pay it no mind. I wanted to ask you\nabout something else.
MID_EV11_051_m01_028: By what means does a simple painter entrap his\nvictims within a picture?
MID_EV11_051_m01_029: There exist magical items called Drake's treasures.\nThey contain terrifying power beyond mortal ken.
MID_EV11_051_m01_030: They take various forms, such as weapons or jewels.\nTheir creator and their total number are unknown.
MID_EV11_051_m01_031: The true nature of these treasures is currently under\ninvestigation by those of us in the Order of Mithras.
MID_EV11_051_m01_032: We have no doubt that the artist's brush recovered\nin Aurora's temple was one of them.
MID_EV11_051_m01_033: Some are weapons, you say... And others are jewels.\nInteresting. Well, please continue to investigate.
MID_EV11_051_m01_034: By your leave, then.
MID_EV11_051_m01_035: Wait a moment. One more thing.
MID_EV11_051_m01_036: This whole incident with the painter... I find your\norder's involvement here a bit questionable.
MID_EV11_051_m01_037: I am grateful for how you revived someone very\ndear to me—my Iliana.
MID_EV11_051_m01_038: Your powers are remarkable. But never forget you\nserve the will of the Dagdan Empire. Now, that is all.
MID_EV11_051_m01_039: *gasp*